@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — A thread coming into existence
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Listing owner" as actor
box "Backend — Barnabas API" #D1FADF
  participant "RequestsController" as controller
end box
box "Backend — Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "AcceptRequestCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "ListingRequest" as request
  participant "MessageThread" as thread
end box
box "Backend — Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Barnabas database" as db
end box

actor -> controller : Accept a pending request
controller -> handler : Send AcceptRequestCommand
handler -> request : Apply the acceptance transition
request --> handler : Status set to Accepted
handler -> thread : Open, naming the request and carrying the listing and both members
thread --> handler : Thread
handler -> db : Save the transition and the thread in one unit of work
note over handler : L2-064 makes the thread a consequence of\nacceptance rather than a separate act. A committed\nacceptance without a thread would leave the\nrequester notified of a decision they cannot act on.
alt the request was still pending
  db --> handler : Commit result
else another caller decided it first
  db --> handler : Conflict on the request's concurrency token,\nor on the unique RequestId of the thread
  handler --> actor : 409 Conflict, with no second thread created
end
handler --> controller : Request and thread identifiers
controller --> actor : The acceptance, offering the thread
@enduml
